Chromium 157.0.8103.30 -> 157.0.8103.44, for the 157.0.8103.30 tarball.

157.0.8103.44 is a tag on the 157 branch (refs/branch-heads/8103) that has
no source tarball (as of 2026-11-03). It has the fixes made after
157.0.8103.30 up to it: those of 157.0.8103.32 to .34 (use-after-frees in
the bookmarks side panel, MojoCdm, chrome.windows.update and
TransitionPseudoElementData; HttpCache range responses; File System Access's
sensitive paths and ~/.cache; the display lock and Length/CalculationValue
tracing fixes; paste sanitization of SVG <use>; Background Fetch keeping CORS
on retry; V8's JSGetTemplateObject, maps, prototypes and Maglev; Skia's
SkRgnBuilder heap out-of-bounds write, SkSL raster pipeline branches and
Graphite's clip inflation and paint keys; ...), and since .34: the NTP
background files written via a temporary file; MediaSource's GOP keyframe
PTS; CacheStorage's legacy cache_dir migration removed; CSSUnparsedValue's
toString; backdrop-filter animations with reference filters not composited;
the Glic hotkey NOTREACHED; the keyframe snapshot use-after-free; the
gainmap decode cache's uninitialized pixels; WebUSB's reset configuration
invalidation turned off by default again (it broke devices after reset);
V8's Promise.any, module star exports, fast API termination, Wasm debug
break and enum cache fixes; ANGLE's Vulkan disabled attributes
use-after-free; and since .41: Blink's CSSSelector rare data marking
barrier; the Sync tab delegate's dependencies outliving it (a
use-after-free); the app menu's zoom announcements; and since .42: the capability
element's icon-only styles gated behind their feature flag; V8's private
name resolution in catch scopes and class heritage eval (two fixes);
SimpleCache's cleanup on key collision; ANGLE's rejection of overlapping
framebuffer layers (and D3D11 fixes).

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags (chromium/src
refs/tags/157.0.8103.30..157.0.8103.44), ANGLE, DevTools, Skia and V8 (the
only dependencies whose DEPS revisions changed; no CIPD/GCS package or
gclient gn arg changed), as served by Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations, CI configuration, PGO pointers, submodule pointer updates,
DEPS.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h and
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h; commit
f37af91d818ffa034fc2d8f1028dd190dab034ed, refs/branch-heads/8103@{#1090}).
Dawn's stamps and build/util/MINIBRANCH don't change.

Checked: applies to the 157.0.8103.30 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
157.0.8103.44; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag; the one new file (Skia's
resources/sksl/runtime_errors/InvalidTypeInStruct.rts) is an SkSL test
source, not generated; the 157.0.8103.30 tarball's non-git files are all
classified (tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

